Z||000000||Jncomutt||07-30-2001||10:05 AM||||I'm looking to replace my entire exhaust system with something that can provide a bit more power.  I plan on running it with no cat. and a free flowing muffler.  <P>The problem I've come across is that I'm not sure what to do for headers.  Who makes/sells a performance set of headers for the 4cyl?  Also I heard that the stock headers that came on the 4cyl? formula? were different and added some low end power and that I might look in these.  Any Ideas or opinions on this?<P>Also, I'm looking for some recommendations anyone might have, or experiences anyone had with what brand headers...  TIA.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||07-30-2001||10:10 AM||||About the only company who makes a header for the 4 cyl is Hooker. They make two models. Only one has a fitting for the O2 sensor. <BR>Don't know anything about any factory "performance" manifolds. The Formula is a V-6, only, and uses the same manifolds as all the other V-6 Fieros.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jncomutt||07-30-2001||10:17 AM||||Yea,thats what I thought about the formula.  I'll try to see if I can find the post and paste the quote.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jncomutt||07-30-2001||10:20 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by c m west:<BR><B>the headers that you have are factory headers. They were designed for the formula 4 cylinder to provide hp increases in mid to low rpm range, verses stock manifolds - do not get rid of these, you will not find anything out on the market that out performs the stock design.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Edit:  Am I confused, or reading this wrong?<p>[This message has been edited by Jncomutt (edited 07-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||07-30-2001||01:01 PM||||Well...<P>I'm confused, too.<P>There were no production 4 cyl Formulas. Period.<P>He might have been making a comparison between the steel tubing manifolds that came on Fieros and the normal cast iron manifolds that come on other cars. <BR>He's still on the Forum. Maybe he can elaborate.<P>He *does* offer 6 cyl headers. They offer greater high RPM performance, with a small loss of torque and HP at low RPMs. (Per dyno tests on 1fst2m6's 2.8)<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 07-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jncomutt||07-30-2001||02:32 PM||||-k-, well I looked on the Holley site and found the 2 different headers they offer.  I'm not sure if I got this right but it seems the difference is that one is a Tri-Y design and one hasn't the o2 sensor.  Also it seems that there is some reducer? that allows for the o2 sensor for the one that doesn't have it.  <P>-k- So if I got that right, what is the difference between the Tri-Y vs not, just the piping design or sumthing??<p>[This message has been edited by Jncomutt (edited 07-30-2001).]||||reg||1
